ory\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them. In 2025 that middle ran 176% of normal for April to May and 44% for November to December. So far in 2026 it opened low, with January to February at 47% and February to March at 48%. Grid 16953 had its driest year in 2010 at 61%.</p>"}
